{"id": "DemZ2NDHbnT", "title": "Video by artandartists_ai", "description": "When you watch a video from America, it doesn't come from space. It comes through the ocean floor. 🌊\n\nAlmost all intercontinental internet traffic runs through cables on the seabed: hair-thin glass fibres carrying light, boosted by repeaters every 50–100 km. In deep water the cable is about as thick as a garden hose; near the shore it's armoured against anchors and fishing nets. India's biggest landing hubs: Mumbai and Chennai.\n\nSend this to someone who thinks the internet is in the sky ☁️\n\nPhotos: Wikimedia Commons (CC BY / CC BY-SA)\n\n#internet #undersea #techexplained #howtechworks #india", "channel": "artandartists_ai", "uploader_id": "17104311819", "uploader": "Art & Artists - AI", "timestamp": 1792250056, "like_count": 3, "comment_count": 0, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-18141153691575820a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 61.177, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQN-O1UjiBYvJMNMR2zAIE648XX62Nvoh49JST3zAQYTcUe4jw7qFvm7_p8FkyI-F0D2WsY4LnRFWnAu1PZKUC9_XiMVKb9IKv4py7M.mp4?_nc_cat=109&_nc_oc=Adoq0v5fQTVOX93vx5uwN5j04uju8JwBSedZtFCUzce6LfjUcceCRBB2Ncb9ng1uuPDK9wGNfsAFCMUHsq9bZebc&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=BWHR1QbwIv0Q7kNvwEor1lv&%3D&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=vwjPtaaVLjE5ZxZ_wgCnVQ&_nc_ss=70689&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&_nc_zt=28&oh=00_AQRbYzTwu3wLZewRcGSrdvSaYChosVHhmyALJnTNnsh4qA&oe=6AF4308E", "manifest_stream_number": 0, "is_dash_periods": true, "protocol": "https", "audio_ext": "m4a", "video_ext": "none", "vbr": 0, "abr": 61.177, "resolution": "audio only", "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/150.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;